<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seewoosagur Ramgoolam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1900">1900</a>–<a href="/years/1985">1985</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seewoosagur Ramgoolam was a Mauritian physician and politician who led the Labour Party and the island's independence movement. He was chief minister and then prime minister when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritius">Mauritius</a> became independent on 12 March 1968, and held office until 1982. He later served as governor-general, and is often called the father of the nation; the main airport bears his name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seewoosagur-ramgoolam.jpg" alt="Seewoosagur Ramgoolam" width="290" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European Communities · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seewoosagur_Ramgoolam,_1970.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
